WEBVTT

00:00.160 --> 00:01.560
Xie Xuan

00:01.640 --> 00:02.720
You lead a unit

00:02.800 --> 00:03.680
Follow me down

00:03.760 --> 00:05.640
To welcome the volunteers into the city

00:05.720 --> 00:07.520
Your general receives orders

00:09.560 --> 00:10.360
Yuanzhi

00:10.440 --> 00:11.160
Here

00:11.240 --> 00:12.907
Send people to the north

00:13.000 --> 00:15.000
To watch for Wunu movements

00:15.080 --> 00:15.360
Your subject

00:15.520 --> 00:16.920
Receives orders

00:32.760 --> 00:34.760
Pay respects to you, sir

00:35.120 --> 00:36.920
Rise, rise

00:43.000 --> 00:51.500
However, the volunteer troops were a motley crew, with some having backgrounds as bandits. Whether driven by fiery tempers or provoked by Wunu spies instigating trouble from within...

00:52.500 --> 00:61.500
Several internal factions, disputing over living quarters, escalated from verbal squabbles into armed brawls, and thereafter attempted to abandon the city in anger.

00:62.500 --> 00:71.500
Just then, the Wunu main camp suddenly deployed troops toward the South Gate, exploiting Yiyang's internal chaos to assault the city and breaching it that very night. Most of the volunteer army scattered like birds and beasts. The Prince of Jin, Sikong Yao, led his troops in a fight to the death, and was personally slain from horseback by Shi Lang.
